# Cloudflare Pages redirects
#
# BLOG-CODE-001 FIX: no explicit passthrough rule is needed for
# /blog/index.json or /blog/{world}/{file}.md — Cloudflare Pages always
# checks for a matching static file BEFORE consulting this file, so real
# static assets under /blog/ are served automatically regardless of the
# rule below. The old `/blog/*  /blog/*  200` rule instead matched (and
# swallowed) the SPA article route /blog/:slug too, since that also starts
# with /blog/ but has no matching static file — on a direct load or hard
# refresh of an article URL, Cloudflare served its platform 404 instead of
# falling through to index.html, so React Router never got a chance to
# mount BlogArticle.tsx. Removed so /blog/:slug falls through correctly.

# React Router - SPA fallback
/*                /index.html       200
